# Design System & Themes

> Paths below are relative to `apps/desktop/`.

Visual language for **Orbit** — cinematic, dark, controller-first, optimized for TV/couch distance.
Inspired by PS5, Nintendo Switch, and Apple TV launchers.

User-facing theme authoring guide: [docs/THEMES.md](THEMES.md).
Example theme: [docs/examples/arcade-neon.json](examples/arcade-neon.json).

---

## Brand

- **Product name:** Orbit
- **Typography:** system font (`-apple-system`) for display + body; game logos are images
- **Tone:** cinematic dark, glass panels, bold focus rings, minimal chrome
- **Target:** fullscreen macOS desktop, viewed from couch distance

---

## Theme system

Orbit has a single shell and look — **Liquid Glass** (`src/themes/MacosShell.tsx`). Themes change image branding and background only. PS5, Switch 2, and the old color variants are retired; saved IDs resolve to `liquid-glass`. Existing JSON fields remain readable, but runtime colors, radii, fonts, blur, and motion always use Liquid Glass.

### Built-in themes

Defined in `src/themes/catalog.ts` (`BUILT_IN_THEMES`). `kind` groups them in Settings:

| Kind | Themes |
| ---- | ------ |
| `color` | `liquid-glass` (default) |
| `game` | `devil-may-cry-5`, `god-of-war`, `cyberpunk-2077`, `zelda-ocarina-of-time`, `gta-v`, `gta-vi`, `zelda-breath-of-the-wild`, `super-mario` |

Game themes use the same packaged logos and backgrounds in the picker and shell, and apply their own palettes. Settings panels span the header width, with narrower side panels framing the scrollable center.

### Branding

- `ThemeBrand` (`src/themes/ThemeBrand.tsx`) renders the header logo: `logoImage` → `<img>`, otherwise the `ORBIT` product wordmark. Legacy text-logo fields are not rendered. Styles live in `src/themes/brand.css`.
- Branded themes (`isBrandedTheme`) render `OrbitMark` — a small uppercase `ORBIT` centered in the footer. The footer's left text is `branding.tagline`.
- `branding.wallpaper` is exposed as `--theme-wallpaper`; the shell sets `data-wallpaper="true"` and paints it behind non-home routes. Home gives the selected game’s hero and cover priority. The theme wallpaper appears while browsing other tabs and when the game has no usable artwork.

### Theme studio

`modules/settings/components/ThemeStudio.tsx` edits a name, game query, image logo, background, and palette. `ImageSearchModal` searches SteamGridDB for logos and adds TheGamesDB, RAWG, and Wikimedia results for backgrounds. The Rust boundary filters metadata and validates downloaded images before caching them locally. Theme Studio opens the picker through the root-level `DrawerProvider`, which portals the left-side Liquid Glass drawer to `document.body` above transformed routes.

### Custom themes

Drop `.json` files into:

```text
~/Library/Application Support/Orbit/themes/
```

Loaded via Tauri `list_custom_themes`, which sanitizes untrusted JSON (see [docs/TAURI.mdc](TAURI.mdc)). Reload from **Settings → Reload custom themes**.

Custom themes with the same `id` as a built-in theme override the built-in entry.

