## Focus & controller styling

Global navigation rings live in `src/components/focus/focus-ring.css`:

- Controller targets use `[data-focused="true"]` under `html[data-navigation-input="controller"]`.
  Every enabled `Focusable` gets a three-pixel inset `--orbit-focus` outline, including
  controls with legacy `noRing` decoration and portaled dialogs. It survives clipped panels.
- Browser `:focus-visible` uses the same ring. Real pointer motion/clicks dismiss
  controller rings; mouse enter events caused by layout or controller scrolling do
  not steal focus. Forced colors use the system highlight.
- Scrollbars hidden globally (controller scroll via focus navigation)
- `color-scheme: dark` on `:root`

Controller glyph hints rendered by `ControllerGlyphs.ts` based on detected family (Xbox / PlayStation / Nintendo).

